# Interview Copilot build rules

When designing or implementing interview assistant / copilot work, treat these as source of truth:

1. `INTERVIEW_COPILOT_BUILD_FLOW.md` — architecture, phases, milestones, Parakeet merge
2. `PRODUCT_PRD_chatgpt_toggle_listener.md` — full feature inventory from the prototype

## Product model

- **One product, two modes:** Studio (full power UI from `chatgpt_toggle_listener.py`) + Live (Parakeet-class floating overlay).
- Shared packages only: `audio`, `stt`, `llm`, `context`, `session`, `prompts`, `screen`, `notes`, `hotkeys`.
- Use Protocols (`AudioSource`, `STTProvider`, `LLMProvider`, `SessionStore`, `PromptStore`). No new monolith.

## How to implement

- Work **one milestone at a time** (see build flow §7). Do not rebuild everything in one pass.
- Keep `chatgpt_toggle_listener.py` as behavior reference until Studio parity is accepted.
- Preserve persistence contracts: `tabs.json`, `chats.json` (AutoSave by **title**), `ui_prefs.json`, `setup_profiles.json`, `sessions/`.

## Privacy stance

- **OK:** exclude overlay from capture, hide Dock, opacity/click-through.
- **Do not build:** Task Manager disguise, cursor spoofing, tab-switch deception, or “undetectable cheating” marketing.

## Platform policy

- **macOS is primary.** Ship Mac features fully first. Windows is an enhancement, never a Mac blocker.
- On OS conflicts: implement Mac path; stub Windows behind `platform/windows/` adapters; track in Windows backlog (build flow §0).
- OS-specific code only in thin adapters (audio cable, picker, capture-exclude, Dock/taskbar). Core packages stay OS-agnostic.
- Hotkeys: Cmd on Mac; mirror with Ctrl on Windows when that adapter is built.

## Defaults

- macOS-first, OpenAI-first, local JSON, Python 3.11+, type hints, main-thread UI updates via `after`.
